# bullmq's package.json lists redis@>=5.0.0 as an OPTIONAL peer dependency
# (it only needs it for a feature we don't use — we already pass it an
# ioredis connection directly, see src/config/queue.js). The project pins
# redis@^4.6.15 for connect-redis (sessions) and rate-limit-redis (rate
# limiting), which are unrelated packages with their own, correct
# requirement on redis v4's client API — connect-redis and rate-limit-redis
# do NOT support redis v5 yet, so upgrading redis instead of doing this
# would break both of those.
#
# npm's default resolver still hard-fails (ERESOLVE) on this conflict even
# though the peer is optional. legacy-peer-deps tells npm to install
# anyway instead of erroring — this is exactly what the failed Render
# build's own error message suggested ("retry with --legacy-peer-deps").
# Verified locally: `npm install` completes cleanly with this file present,
# and bullmq, ioredis, redis, connect-redis, and rate-limit-redis all load.
legacy-peer-deps=true
